cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Synthetic Data Distillation from Large Language Models for
  Turkish Abstractive News Summarization
message: >-
  If you use this software or its released predictions, please cite the
  conference paper below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Çalışkan
    given-names: Çağan
    affiliation: Izmir Institute of Technology
    email: caliskancagan2005@gmail.com
repository-code: https://github.com/cagancaliskan/turkish-summarization-distillation
abstract: >-
  A 300M-parameter student (mT5-small with LoRA adapters) is distilled from
  ~10,000 synthetic summaries generated by GPT-4o-mini and Claude Haiku 4.5,
  and evaluated against zero-shot, human-supervised and teacher baselines on
  MLSUM-TR and, out of domain, on TR-News. The student recovers 92.6% of its
  teacher's stemmed ROUGE-1 in-domain and significantly outperforms both
  teachers out of domain. Includes a pre-registered statistical protocol
  (bootstrap confidence intervals, paired randomization tests, TOST
  equivalence testing), a post-hoc bias analysis, and the quantification of a
  systematic mT5 decoding artifact that had depressed every metric the small
  models were scored on.
keywords:
  - abstractive summarization
  - Turkish NLP
  - knowledge distillation
  - parameter-efficient fine-tuning
  - LoRA
  - mT5
  - low-resource languages
